ciation subtracts: use (1 − i), not (1 + i).","qs":[{"text":"A car worth R250 000, reducing balance 18% p.a., after 4 years","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Value (R)","a":"113030.44","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Use A = P(1 − i)ⁿ.","steps":"1. Formula (reducing-balance depreciation): A = P(1 − i)ⁿ<br>2. A = 250 000(1 − 0,18)⁴ = 250 000 × 0,82⁴<br>3. ≈ R113 030,44"},{"text":"A tractor worth R400 000, straight-line 10% p.a., after 6 years","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Value (R)","a":"160000.00","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"1 − 0,6","steps":"1. Formula (straight-line depreciation): A = P(1 − in)<br>2. A = 400 000(1 − 0,1 × 6) = 400 000 × 0,4<br>3. = R160 000,00"},{"text":"Straight-line: R60 000 falls to R24 000 in 4 years. Find the rate.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Rate (%)","a":"15","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Find the total drop in value first.","steps":"1. Formula (straight-line depreciation): A = P(1 − in)<br>2. 24 000 = 60 000(1 − 4i), so 1 − 4i = 0,4<br>3. 4i = 0,6, so i = 0,15 = 15%"}]}